{
  "dom_id": "step-q183349",
  "name": "Question 12",
  "problem": "$\\,$ If $x\\in N,$ then  $x$ is positive.\n\nWhich of the following is logically equivalent to the conditional predicate above?",
  "worked_solution": "Let's denote by $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ the following predicates:\n\n- $P(x):$ $x\\in N.$\n\n- $Q(x):$ $x$ is positive.\n\nThen, our initial sentence can be written as $P(x)\u21d2Q(x),$ which is logically equivalent to \n\n$$\n\u00acP(x)\u2228Q(x).\n$$\n\nThe negation of $P(x)$ can be written as\n\n- $\u00acP(x):$ $x\\notin N.$\n\nTherefore, the given sentence is logically equivalent to the following:\n\n$\\,$ $x\\notin N,$ or $x$ is positive.",
